//! Batch 333 -- the sgl-nvidia-mega megakernel-serving `kernel_opt` distill
//! (Plan 341 / Research 371).
//!
//! Source: `sgl-project/sgl-nvidia-mega` @ `c396f2ab6c7e779af326321ef75fb5b6008e6165`
//! (Apache-2.0; HEAD 2026-11-02; shallow clone read at the pin + removed at the
//! verdict commit, re-verified at this batch's clone). `SGLang`'s official `NVIDIA`
//! megakernel plugin: per covered model, the small-batch decode step as ONE
//! co-resident launch handing outputs through Lamport mailboxes and `PDL`.
//! Per-file provenance: `markov.cu` = `vLLM` project + `NVIDIA` (modified from the
//! original: "up to 64 request rows, hoisted step parameters, fail-stop waits");
//! `common/sync.py` = `FlashInfer` + `vLLM` (adapted from `flashinfer-ai/flashinfer@139af6f6`
//! mnnvl `CuTe` DSL primitives, "modified from its original version (cross-GPU
//! wait deadlines)"); `mkd_xchg.cu` = `NVIDIA`, adapted from `SGLang`
//! `mkd_draft_xchg.cuh` (branch nvidia/qwen35-agentx-gb300), device code
//! unchanged. Hardware regime: `GB300`/`SM103` + `NVLink` symmetric-memory peer
//! buffers + `multimem` + `PDL` (`sm_90`+) -- silicon the workspace does not own
//! (the B110 precedent: these rules serve USER code on hardware we do not
//! have). The repo ships NO perf claims (its own README: "bounded functional
//! and quality evidence; it does not claim performance") -- provenance, never
//! bars. Kills recorded in Research 371 (order-preserving key packing =
//! `gpu_20`'s positive instance; flag formats = `gpu_30` x2; wait ladder = `gpu_118`;
//! walk residency = `gpu_23`; two-shot rank-order reduce = `gpu_142`'s numeric
//! contract, a THIRD independent implementation; `PDL` chains = `gpu_23`+`gpu_111`).
//! Product-coverage: seeds the `SGLang` family (was EMPTY -- 0 sourced rules).
//! Batch 333 / Plan 341 / Research 371.
//!
//! Batch 335 APPEND (Plan 344 / Research 373) -- the mxfp4-int8-m5 W4A8
//! distill (rules 3-5 below): source `shinyoungkang1/mxfp4-int8-m5` @
//! `3d060c616738b980155f712a5e5505caeb32b7c2` (MIT; HEAD 2026-11-04; cloned
//! at the pin per batch, removed at the landing). The paper's own code
//! release for Integer-Exact Microscaling (arXiv 2611.00486, CC BY 4.0):
//! on Apple M5 Neural Accelerators (Metal 4 `matmul2d`, INT8 x INT8 at
//! 1.79-1.98x FP16), a row of MXFP4 weights is EXACTLY one INT8 vector
//! times one power-of-two scale iff its block exponents span <= 3 -- one
//! exact INT8 GEMM, one rescale per output, no per-block work in the
//! reduction; 97.9-99.97% of rows across seven models comply unmodified.
//! Kills recorded in Research 373 (grouped-GEMM prefix-sum dispatch = the
//! D-family owned; `GROUP_M` swizzle = l2-grouped owned; E2M1 half bit-trick
//! = LUT/byte-perm class; exact-int GEMV contract = the `gpu_106`/`gpu_142`
//! composition). Corroborations (record, never re-land): the GPU-timing
//! lock + disturbed-run rejection = the box-state discipline externalized
//! (`tools/gpu_timing.sh` 'a lock that gives timing runs the GPU to
//! themselves'); bit-identical parity as the correctness axis throughout.
//! Product-coverage: extends the MLX ecosystem family (first paper-first
//! member). Batch 335 / Plan 344 / Research 373.

